,"updated_at":"2026-07-01T07:31:31Z","body":"  > - For example, it could be argued that a \"custom\" `pick_random` could also reside in **RandomNumberGenerator**, for reasons similar to https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11853\n> \n> \n\nWe need to decide which pattern we want for all of these functions. Either adding default arguments to the already exisiting arrays functions, or make new functions that take in arrays as parameters that reside inside `RandomNumberGenerator`. Personally I prefer the former since it makes more sense with the more OOP approach of godot, while the latter is more c-style.\n\nIt will be sad if the first PR out of these that gets merged will be the standard that the other need to follow, but won't be nessecarily the better architecture-wise.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4851505526/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]